[{"id":2679621722,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ft8ha","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks!\r\n\r\nThis is really great. :-) I like how it unifies some of the manifest changes (metadata and features) in both Gradle and APK-based builds.\r\n\r\nI tested doing an OpenXR build using just an APK-based export (with an APK built from https://github.com/godot-sdk-integrations/godot-meta-toolkit/pull/15) and it worked great. I also \"decompiled\" the APK with apktool and the manifest all looks good.\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm not sure this is a good one for cherry-picking, at least not right away. There's the virtual method that's added here (which we don't usually add in patch releases), but it also just seems like a lot of changes. Maybe wait until it's gotten a bunch more testing in 4.5-dev releases first? I know there's some fixes mixed in here too - if some of them don't depend on the feature changes, maybe they could be extracted to another PR?","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103173#pullrequestreview-2679621722","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.